          "type": "open",
          "q": "Using elementary column transformations, find the inverse of A = [[2, −6], [1, −2]].",
          "answer": "|A| = −4 + 6 = 2, so A⁻¹ exists. Write A = AI.\nC₂ → C₂ + 3C₁: [[2, 0], [1, 1]] = A[[1, 3], [0, 1]].\nC₁ → C₁ − C₂: [[2, 0], [0, 1]] = A[[−2, 3], [−1, 1]].\nC₁ → C₁/2: [[1, 0], [0, 1]] = A[[−1, 3], [−½, 1]].\nA⁻¹ = [[−1, 3], [−½, 1]].",
          "years": [
            "October 2024"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "4.2",
          "type": "open",
          "q": "Using the matrix method, solve 2x − 3y + 5z = 16, 3x + 2y − 4z = −4, x + y − 2z = −3.",
          "answer": "|A| = 2(−4 + 4) + 3(−6 + 4) + 5(3 − 2) = 0 − 6 + 5 = −1.\nCofactors: C₁₁ = 0, C₁₂ = 2, C₁₃ = 1; C₂₁ = −1, C₂₂ = −9, C₂₃ = −5; C₃₁ = 2, C₃₂ = 23, C₃₃ = 13.\nA⁻¹ = −adj A = −[[0, −1, 2], [2, −9, 23], [1, −5, 13]].\nX = A⁻¹B: x = −(0 + 4 − 6) = 2; y = −(32 + 36 − 69) = 1; z = −(16 + 20 − 39) = 3.\nx = 2, y = 1, z = 3.",
          "years": [
            "April 2025"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "4.3",
          "type": "open",
          "q": "Using the matrix method, solve x + 2y + 3z = 0, 2x + 3y + 2z = −2, 3x − 3y + 4z = 13.",
          "answer": "|A| = 1(12 + 6) − 2(8 − 6) + 3(−6 − 9) = 18 − 4 − 45 = −31.\nadj A = [[18, −17, −5], [−2, −5, 4], [−15, 9, −1]].\nX = A⁻¹B = (−1/31)[18·0 − 17(−2) − 5·13, −2·0 − 5(−2) + 4·13, −15·0 + 9(−2) − 13]\n= (−1/31)[−31, 62, −31] = [1, −2, 1].\nx = 1, y = −2, z = 1.",
          "years": [
            "October 2025"
          ]
        }
