          "type": "open",
          "q": "If A = [[1, 1, 1], [1, 2, −3], [2, −1, 3]], find A⁻¹ and use it to solve x + y + z = −2, x + 2y − 3z = 12, 2x − y + 3z = −13.",
          "answer": "|A| = 1(6 − 3) − 1(3 + 6) + 1(−1 − 4) = 3 − 9 − 5 = −11.\nCofactors: C₁₁ = 3, C₁₂ = −9, C₁₃ = −5; C₂₁ = −4, C₂₂ = 1, C₂₃ = 3; C₃₁ = −5, C₃₂ = 4, C₃₃ = 1.\nadj A = [[3, −4, −5], [−9, 1, 4], [−5, 3, 1]]; A⁻¹ = (−1/11) adj A.\nX = A⁻¹B with B = [−2, 12, −13]:\nx = (−1/11)(−6 − 48 + 65) = (−1/11)(11) = −1.\ny = (−1/11)(18 + 12 − 52) = (−1/11)(−22) = 2.\nz = (−1/11)(10 + 36 − 13) = (−1/11)(33) = −3.\nx = −1, y = 2, z = −3.",
          "years": [
            "April 2026"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "5.2",
          "type": "open",
          "q": "Using the matrix method, solve 3x + y + z = 1, 2x + 2z = 0, 5x − y + 2z = 4.",
          "answer": "|A| = 3(0 + 2) − 1(4 − 10) + 1(−2 − 0) = 6 + 6 − 2 = 10.\nCofactors: C₁₁ = 2, C₁₂ = 6, C₁₃ = −2; C₂₁ = −3, C₂₂ = 1, C₂₃ = 8; C₃₁ = 2, C₃₂ = −4, C₃₃ = −2.\nadj A = [[2, −3, 2], [6, 1, −4], [−2, 8, −2]].\nX = (1/10)adj A · [1, 0, 4] = (1/10)[2 + 8, 6 − 16, −2 − 8] = [1, −1, −1].\nx = 1, y = −1, z = −1.",
